WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.009
Making it through the zombie apocalypse means
putting your survival instincts to the test—and

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:08.080
putting your weekly manicure on hold until
things blow over.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.680
But while these survivors on The Walking Dead
look like they haven't seen a hot shower in

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.589
a while, the actors playing them are doing
just fine in the personal hygiene department.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:19.450
"I hope you don't mind me saying this, but
you smell very very good."

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.450
"Oh thank you!"

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.450
"… do you shampoo?"

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.450
"I do, I do!"

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.009
Stick with us while we check out what the
cast of AMC's The Walking Dead looks like

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:27.080
in real life.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:32.520
And in case you were wondering, there are some minor undead spoilers for Walking Dead seasons 1-6 ahead.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.800
Andrew Lincoln

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:39.261
As the first character introduced in the series
premiere of The Walking Dead in 2010, Rick

00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:43.160
Grimes started his undead odyssey as your
typical clean-cut Sheriff's Deputy.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.740
But being constantly brutalized and watching
your friends and loved ones succumb to the

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.930
horrors of the apocalypse can change a man—and
Rick's difficulty coming to grips with the

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:56.000
world's encroaching chaos is physically embodied
by his hair and beard, which grew increasingly

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.079
more disheveled before reaching its magnificent
peak in Season 5.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:04.220
Fortunately, the dashing Andrew Lincoln has
little in common with his tormented character

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.080
beyond his rugged good looks.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.970
Where Rick is a hard-boiled guardian, Lincoln
is a fun-loving guy who likes to play pranks

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:14.750
on his castmates — and who keeps his facial
forest well under control.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.320
Norman Reedus

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.300
Daryl Dixon is more comfortable on a hog than
in an armored car, and his appearance parallels

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.490
his no-nonsense approach to survival.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:26.840
With scraggly locks and that trademark squint,
Daryl's look is a post-apocalyptic take on

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.040
biker chic… except when he's wearing this
fabulous poncho.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.550
In real life, Reedus is pretty much indistinguishable
from his character… albeit with slightly

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.610
less dirt and blood caked on his clothing.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:42.640
It doesn't take much effort to transform Reedus—who,
like Daryl, really takes his motorcycles seriously—into

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.910
his fictional, walker-whacking counterpart.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.470
But in real life, Reedus is a sweetheart who
loves to surprise his castmates with kisses.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.870
Lots of kisses.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.310
Chandler Riggs

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.970
This young actor has undergone major changes
since Season 1—both as a result of the nightmare

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:01.000
unfolding around him, but also as a result
of puberty, which is a whole different kind

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.000
of nightmare.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.090
Riggs was first cast as Carl at the tender
age of 10, and seven years later, he's got

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.600
some battle scars — like the gaping hole
where his eyeball used to be.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.560
"Have you seen it?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.860
Have you looked in the mirror? That is gross as hell!"

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.700
But take away the bandage (or the gruesome
prosthetic), knock off the cowboy hat, and

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.820
here's what Chandler looks like in real life
— complete with that signature shag haircut,

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.540
which he's contractually obligated to keep.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.070
Danai Gurira

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:32.090
This sword-wielding warrior took the screen
by storm in season 3 — and forget what we

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.780
said about putting fashion on hold in the
apocalypse, because Michonne kicks walker

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.380
ass in style, slicing and dicing in distressed
skinny jeans and her signature sleeveless

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.480
leather vest.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.990
Gurira really brings her character to life—so
it came as a minor shock to super fans everywhere

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.431
when they realized that the actress has always
worn her hair short, even shaving it for her

00:02:50.431 --> 00:02:52.400
role in Marvel's Black Panther film.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.830
That's right—those locs are a wig, and while
they're not the most comfortable thing to

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.230
wear while filming in the Georgia heat, Gurira
says they have their perks.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:04.300
"It's one of the most user-friendly styles a black girl can have during the apocalypse."

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.320
Steven Yeun

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.140
Glenn may be best remembered for the skull
crack heard around the world, but he was also

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.319
the group's moral compass.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.741
His practical, no-frills style was an echo
of his attitude — but in real life, actor

00:03:14.741 --> 00:03:18.980
Steven Yeun is a much more dapper dresser,
and much less likely to show up covered in

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:19.980
zombie guts.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.840
At his most casual, though, he still has a
lot in common with his character, right down

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.590
to the baseball cap.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.100
Melissa McBride

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.069
Thanks to her friendship with early Walking
Dead showrunner Frank Darabont, this casting

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.880
director-turned-actress was a shoo-in for
the role of Carol.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.070
A fan favorite for her cunning and loyalty
to the team, Carol's short, silver hair has

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.910
become an emblem of her journey from an abused
wife to an ice-cold killer.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.910
When it's time to transform McBride into a
camera-ready survivor, it's just a question

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.020
of mussing up her hair, popping a rifle in
her hands, and smearing a little dirt on her

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.020
face.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.490
The rest is pure acting talent.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:53.720
Lauren Cohan

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.120
From farmer's daughter to tough-as-nails widow,
Cohan's character Maggie has transformed since

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.480
her season two debut into a savvy leader of
the Hilltop's militia — and traded in her

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.780
farm-friendly look for baseball caps, hunting
jackets, and handgun holsters.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.500
But in real life, Lauren Cohan is all glitz
and glamour—at least compared to her kneecap-busting

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.500
counterpart.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.190
Cohan, who modeled for Richard Branson's failed
apparel company Virgin Clothing before hitting

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.739
it big in Hollywood, regularly opts for designer
clothing and elegant makeup rather than the

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:23.060
apocalyptic rags in Maggie's wardrobe.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.940
Hey—nobody wants to take their work home
with them, right?

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:26.970
Lennie James

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.710
Between his mental breakdown, his fling with
pacifism, and his chaotic collapse back into

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.370
homicide after Richard's betrayal of the Kingdom,
Morgan is a ticking time bomb in makeshift

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.370
armor.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:40.280
But actor Lennie James, on the other hand,
is one dapper son of a gun.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.632
After graduating from Guildhall School of
Music and Drama, the English — yes, English!

00:04:43.632 --> 00:04:47.630
— actor had a long career on screen before
finding his way to The Walking Dead, although

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.950
there's at least one coveted role he still
hasn't gotten to play.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.900
"I would like to have been Batman."

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:58.020
Meanwhile, like the caped crusader, Morgan's
looking a little wild around the eyes these

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.780
days — but James is out and about rocking
a pair of dark frames and a single earring.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.270
Jeffrey Dean Morgan

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:09.370
Whether you hate to love him or love to hate
him, this man changed the game as the zombie

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.050
apocalypse's Louisville-slugger-swinging sociopath
— and we'll be darned if he doesn't look

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.990
awfully stylish, even in that dastardly debut
that had fans sobbing into their barf bags.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:22.370
In his role as Negan, Morgan rocks a leather
jacket that suggests a pre-apocalypse penchant

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.410
for punk rock and a red scarf that has inspired
countless articles speculating about its meaning.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:31.790
In real life, Jeffrey Dean Morgan doesn't
share the same sensibilities as his character—

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.360
and with good reason, since he's confessed
that he finds the role itself extremely emotionally

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.360
taxing.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.660
That might be why he grows out his whiskers
during The Walking Dead's off season, the

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.450
better to distance himself from the villainous,
clean-shaven Negan.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.450
Josh McDermitt

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:50.680
As the zombie drama's most knowledgeable survivor,
Eugene can make poison and craft bullets—

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.360
and betray his friends to become Negan's right-hand
man.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.389
Happily, the actor who plays him is the total
opposite of his TV counterpart.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:02.300
Let's do this one rapid-fire: Actor Josh McDermitt's
natural hair color is blond, that's not his

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:06.501
real voice, and the mullet he sported when
he first arrived on the show was a wig—

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:10.889
"I have this other acting job called my personal
life that I not wanna have the mullet on."

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:14.770
— although recent photos suggest that he's
starting to embrace Eugene's hairdo as a way

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.520
of life, if not his penchant for cargo vests.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.970
But most importantly, Josh McDermitt is nothing
like the cowardly Eugene, which means that

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:25.620
if you see him on the street you should be
nice and not yell at him.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.710
Khary Payton

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:31.950
As the show's scenery-chewing community-theatre-actor-turned
King, Payton has undergone a dramatic makeover

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.870
himself to play Ezekiel one of the series'
most polarizing characters.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:40.320
The King sports a mane of gray dreadlocks
and regal garments fit for an Elder Scrolls

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.070
emperor— a look that's totally in contrast
with Payton's stripped-down, casual aesthetic.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:49.419
In real life, this actor keeps things simple—with
a shaved head and the best beard this side

00:06:49.419 --> 00:06:50.889
of Game of Thrones.

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.300
Christian Serratos

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.570
It's hard to believe that Christian Serratos
shared a cafeteria with the Twilight vampires

00:06:56.570 --> 00:07:01.949
before stealing our hearts as the feisty Rosita
Espinosa when she joined the cast in season

00:07:01.949 --> 00:07:02.949
4.

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:06.580
After the decimation of two of her besties
at the hands of Negan, Rosita quickly became

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.729
an outspoken proponent of slaughtering the
Saviors— and swapped out her trendy traveling

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:13.910
outfit and youthful pigtails for a more practical
look.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.400
Meanwhile, off-camera, Serratos is right at
home on the red carpet and usually wears designer

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.320
duds that would be totally impractical in
a zombie apocalypse.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.509
Michael Cudlitz

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.690
Let's face it: Abraham's got a face only a
mother could love.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.979
Well, and Rosita.

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:28.979
And Sasha.

00:07:28.979 --> 00:07:29.979
And his late wife Ellen…

00:07:29.979 --> 00:07:32.350
OK, so the big lug actually gets a lot of
love.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:37.100
But between the signature scowl, the iconic
mustache, and the orange box cut, Abraham's

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.580
lucky he's got charm — and a gift for self-expression.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:45.770
"Maybe I'll let you shave me down all over
- dolphin smooth."

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:49.770
In real life, fans of Abe will be shocked
to learn that actor Michael Cudlitz is actually

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:54.270
a natural blond— and he's nowhere near as
averse to sleeves as The Walking Dead costume

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.139
department would have you believe.

00:07:56.139 --> 00:07:57.479
Austin Amelio

00:07:57.479 --> 00:08:01.550
After a botched attempt at stealing medical
supplies, Amelio's character Dwight had a

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:05.240
close encounter with a burning-hot iron—
which is Negan's preferred punishment for

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:08.460
disloyal Saviors, when he doesn't just straight-up
beat them to death.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.050
Fortunately, that melted face is purely prosthetic.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:15.360
In real life, Austin Amelio lacks both the
disfiguring injury and the haunted look of

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.540
his Walking Dead character.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:20.430
And when he's not cleaning up to walk the
red carpet, his preferred style is skater

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.820
chic, in keeping with his first career as
a semi-professional skateboarder.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.759
Sonequa Martin Green

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:30.910
Before being cast on Star Trek: Discovery,
this actress spent five seasons playing Sasha

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.149
— the Walking Dead character who just couldn't
catch a break.

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:38.579
First, she lost her brother Tyreese; then
her boyfriend Bob met a bad end; and, finally,

00:08:38.579 --> 00:08:41.389
her romance with Abraham was cut short before
it could even begin.

00:08:41.389 --> 00:08:45.980
At the end of Season Six, Sasha sacrificed
her life to help turn the tables on the Scavengers

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.959
and the Saviors… and to boldly go where
no man had gone before, of course.

00:08:49.959 --> 00:08:54.800
In real life, Martin-Green is just as devoted
to her family as Sasha, particularly the son

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.790
she gave birth to shortly after the show's
fifth season.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.550
But don't be fooled by her laid-back apocalypse
style and permanent ponytail; off set, this

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:06.649
actress is all about experimental glamour
and gravity-defying hairstyles.

00:09:06.649 --> 00:09:07.649
David Morrissey

00:09:07.649 --> 00:09:11.879
This actor's performance as Philip Blake—better
known as the Governor—reminded audiences

00:09:11.879 --> 00:09:15.329
that zombies weren't the only thing to be
afraid of during the end days.

00:09:15.329 --> 00:09:19.759
With a clean-cut appearance that masked some
seriously twisted sensibilities, the Governor

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:24.110
was a sinister figure even before he put on
the iconic eyepatch that marked him as a true

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:25.110
villain.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:28.870
But while David Morrissey is just as handsome
as his Walking Dead character in real life,

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.200
the similarities end there.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.379
For one thing, he's a much snappier dresser.

00:09:32.379 --> 00:09:36.240
But more importantly, the British actor is
such a warm, friendly fellow that his co-stars

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.660
considered it a privilege to be hunted by
him.

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:42.550
"That was the funnest scene, I think, when
he was trying to kill me"

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:43.550
Seth Gilliam

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:47.740
For all of his errors in judgement, Gilliam's
Father Gabriel has since turned out to be

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:52.199
a loyal, solid moral force within Rick's band
of survivors — not to mention the only person

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.700
capable of frightening Negan just by showing
up.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.360
"Hoooly crap!

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.640
You are creepy as s---!"

00:10:00.649 --> 00:10:04.560
Needless to say, Seth Gilliam doesn't wear
a clerical collar in real life — but he's

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.249
no stranger to playing characters who share
Gabriel's complexity.

00:10:07.249 --> 00:10:11.480
You might have seen him on The Wire as Sergeant
Ellis Carver, who epitomized the potential

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:15.679
for positive change both as a human being
and as an officer of the law.

00:10:15.679 --> 00:10:17.259
Pollyanna McIntosh

00:10:17.259 --> 00:10:21.699
Season seven of The Walking Dead saw the introduction
of a new group to the mix—the Scavengers,

00:10:21.699 --> 00:10:25.910
a group of survivors with a love of recycling
and all things hooded.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.910
Unfortunately, this crew eventually betrayed
Rick's collective during a massive shoot-out

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:30.990
with the Saviors.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.410
But we're glad they showed up just for the
pleasure of meeting McIntosh's character,

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:39.179
an oddball named Jadis who collects junkyard
art and staunchly refuses to conjugate her

00:10:39.179 --> 00:10:40.179
verbs.

00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:42.829
"Our guns to take our deal still on."

00:10:42.829 --> 00:10:48.290
Offscreen, McIntosh is practically unrecognizable
as Jadis, except for the blunt bangs and post-apocalyptic

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.279
dye job that somehow manages to still look
glamorous.

00:10:51.279 --> 00:10:55.410
And unlike her character, the actress speaks
in complete sentences — and with an English

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.410
accent.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:58.230
"It was really exciting from start to finish."

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.230
Thanks for watching!

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.430
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.539
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

